    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1064">

                <pb facs="1215" n="1103" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg1103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 (China) Thrift Corp./43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-12T18:00:00+08:00">October 12, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 12—8 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Embassy’s 49, October 11, 3 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d1064-f1"/> Following
                    telegram has been received from the Consul General at Harbin: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“41, October 12, 1 p.m. My October 11, 11 a.m. My statement was put in
                            eight local newspapers of yesterday and today’s issues. I yesterday
                            requested the Thriftcor Bank to cease flying the American flag.</p>
                        <pb facs="1216" n="1104" xml:id="pg1104"/>
                        <list>
                            <label>2.</label>
                            <item>The Japanese controlled Russian edited <hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Harbin Times</hi> editorially states that the fact that the
                                American Government allowed the Thriftcor Bank to claim American
                                nationality and fly the flag of the American Government for a number
                                of years and then disclaimed responsibility for the liquidation of
                                the Thriftcor Bank give rise to question as to the status of other
                                American enterprises in Harbin.</item>
                            <label>3.</label>
                            <item>The National City Bank states that it has paid out today about
                                100,000 local dollars as a result of transactions caused by the
                                above editorial statement. I understand that within the last week
                                the National City Bank has paid out about 1,000,000 local
                                dollars.</item>
                            <label>4.</label>
                            <item>I am today addressing a letter to the National City Bank
                                confirming currency of its registration in this Consulate General.
                                The National City Bank will publish that letter.”</item>
                        </list>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
